# Whitespace rules for `git diff --check` (see scripts/verify-whitespace.sh).
#
# Everything gets git's default checks: trailing whitespace, space-before-tab,
# and a missing newline at end of file.
#
# Markdown is the one exception, and only for trailing space. Two spaces at the
# end of a Markdown line are a hard line break — real syntax, used deliberately
# in the master plan's header block — and git cannot tell an intentional pair
# from an accidental one. Flagging them would push a gate toward either
# reformatting a document somebody wrote on purpose or being switched off.
# space-before-tab and the missing-final-newline check still apply.
*.md whitespace=-trailing-space
